Open Mapple: the XNU kernel, common to Qualcomm phones.

- Apple's XNU (xnu-8796.141.3), libpthread (514.100.2), HFS (627.100.6) and IOHIDFamily headers: Apple Public Source License 2.0
  (APPLE_LICENSE). Changes to Apple's files are under the same licence, and Apple's notices stay in them.
- ios-sweet (github.com/dipa-studio/ios-sweet): its patch series for the Redmi Note 10 Pro, by dipa-studio and damjankakak3, with changes
  from legendxdevil and 2010475745xie in the repository. The files it adds are MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 dipa-studio; its changes to Apple's
  files are APSL 2.0.
- ios-sweet-pixel, branch sunfish (github.com/hellagarage/ios-sweet-pixel): the Pixel 4a and Adreno 618 work of frokfrdk and hellagarage
  (one commit under another name), on top of ios-sweet. MIT.
- ios-fajita (github.com/edi194/ios-fajita) and ios-fuxi (github.com/bangprovn/ios-fuxi): their changes to Apple's files only (APSL 2.0),
  by edi194 and bangprovn. Neither repository has a licence of its own; nothing else of theirs is here. Their pieces are replayed with
  their authors and say so in an Imported-from: line.
- darwin-xnu-build (github.com/blacktop/darwin-xnu-build): its build fixes. MIT, Copyright (c) 2023-2025 blacktop.
- BearSSL (Thomas Pornin), libkern/crypto/sweet_bearssl/: MIT, its LICENSE.txt.
- iokit/Kernel/arm/sweet_msm.h: the structures of Linux's msm DRM interface (include/uapi/drm/msm_drm.h, Copyright (C) 2013 Red Hat,
  Rob Clark), MIT, notice kept in the file.

